{"name":"Fieldstone","hex":"#807e77","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"Fieldstone","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Proper noun","definitions":["A suburb of Melbourne in the City of Melton, Victoria, Australia"]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/Fieldstone"}],"entries":[{"title":"Fieldstone","blocks":[{"text":"Fieldstone is a naturally occurring type of stone, which lies at or near the surface of the Earth. Fieldstone is a nuisance for farmers seeking to expand their land under cultivation, but at some point it began to be used as a construction material. Strictly speaking, it is stone collected from the surface of fields where it occurs naturally. Collections of fieldstones which have been removed from arable land or pasture to allow for more effective agriculture are called clearance cairns."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/20/Lesesteinhaufen%2C_K%C3%B6nigswald%2C_Potsdam.jpg/330px-Lesesteinhaufen%2C_K%C3%B6nigswald%2C_Potsdam.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Fieldstone","wikidata":"Q1402843"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/53/Haselberg_Feldsteinmauer_frontal.jpg/500px-Haselberg_Feldsteinmauer_frontal.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/53/Haselberg_Feldsteinmauer_frontal.jpg/1280px-Haselberg_Feldsteinmauer_frontal.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/53/Haselberg_Feldsteinmauer_frontal.jpg/500px-Haselberg_Feldsteinmauer_frontal.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Fieldstone wall in Wriezen-Haselberg, Germany","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AHaselberg_Feldsteinmauer_frontal.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/comm